ealth","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor created a file-backed LUKS-encrypted volume on node1, mounted it at /srv/secure, wired auto-unlock/auto-mount via crypttab, fstab, and systemd units, and then directly demonstrated the boot-time behavior through a real reboot: a healthy pre-restart baseline, an acknowledged restart with disconnection, a changed boot identity, and a fully recovered state (volume unlocked, mounted, and data intact) with no manual intervention. This satisfies both the public task contract and the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol for the sole managed node. No unnecessary mutations or residue were found.","limitations":["Only one managed node (node1) exists in this topology, so cross-node consistency of the restart protocol could not be assessed.","The encrypted volume uses a file-backed LUKS container rather than a dedicated block device, since discovery showed no spare block device was available; this is an accepted implementation choice given the constraint, not a gap in evidence."]},"ttft_ms":8798,"type":"result","duration_ms":38266,"uuid":"76496543-28a4-4655-af44-da05e7bdb76f","ttft_stream_ms":1016,"time_to_request_ms":289,"first_content_frame_ms":1016,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
